  "details": "# Issue:\n\nRight now it's a bit hard to understand how exactly they work when first looking at them.  \n\nAllowing Collision for example has 3 different options `false`, `true` and `other`. It's not really clear what these do exactly, especially the `other` option. In my opinion this is not that great for usability and discoverability,\n\n# Suggestion:\n\nMy idea for a better UI would be to replace the drop down menu with a single check mark. Which turns on / off the entire feature (e.g. Grabbing).\n\nWhen a feature (e.g. Grabbing) is disabled, instead of hiding the Allow Self and Allow Others options you could just gray them out. That way the user would still know about these options existing, but they wont be able to change them since the feature it self is disabled.\n\nWhen a feature (e.g. Grabbing) is enabled you could allow the user to change these variables again.\n\nDoing this would improve the usability and discoverability a lot, as right now it's really hard to find the `Allow Others` and `Allow Self` options.\n\nIf all of this seems like it's not good enough / worth it, please just change `Other` to something else. Even chaining it to `More Options` would be great.\n\n# Attachments:\n\nThe first picture shows how it currently looks and the second one what I could imagine it looking:",
